From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Show the DeX taskbar by pushing past the bottom edge, not by resting there

In a fullscreen DeX app, Samsung reveals the hidden taskbar once a mouse or touchpad cursor stays
in the bottom 22 px for 500 ms, so games that keep the cursor low keep popping it up. Pointer
events from a mouse or touchpad now count only downward movement (AXIS_RELATIVE_Y, which keeps
counting while the cursor is pinned to the edge) inside that strip, and the taskbar shows once it
adds up to 300 px within 500 ms of the first downward move there: a short flick down. Touch swipes
from the bottom edge go through detectSwipe and still show it at once.

diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/SystemGesturesPointerEventListener.smali b/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/SystemGesturesPointerEventListener.smali
index 5627883..fbc5882 100644
--- a/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/SystemGesturesPointerEventListener.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/SystemGesturesPointerEventListener.smali
@@ -41,6 +41,10 @@
 
 .field public mMouseHoveringAtTop:Z
 
+.field public mOnigiriPush:F
+
+.field public mOnigiriPushStart:J
+
 .field public mMultiWindowEdgeDetector:Lcom/samsung/android/multiwindow/MultiWindowEdgeDetector;
 
 .field public mSwipeDistanceThreshold:I
@@ -384,6 +388,20 @@
     goto :goto_0
 
     :cond_1
+    # A mouse or touchpad shows the taskbar by pushing past the bottom edge, not by resting there.
+    const/16 v0, 0x2002
+
+    invoke-virtual {p1, v0}, Landroid/view/MotionEvent;->isFromSource(I)Z
+
+    move-result v0
+
+    if-eqz v0, :cond_onigiri_0
+
+    invoke-virtual {p0, p1}, Lcom/android/server/wm/SystemGesturesPointerEventListener;->onigiriPushPastBottom(Landroid/view/MotionEvent;)V
+
+    return-void
+
+    :cond_onigiri_0
     iget-boolean v0, p0, Lcom/android/server/wm/SystemGesturesPointerEventListener;->mMouseHoveringAtBottom:Z
 
     if-nez v0, :cond_2
@@ -446,6 +464,109 @@
     return-void
 .end method
 
